t in the  absence of a history of violence or any  of the other risk factors it is  impossible to identify who will go on to  become violent for every individual who  goes on a shooting rampage there are a  hundred or perhaps more individuals who  also had  disturbed relationships with teachers  parents authorities want to know what  caused the alleged gunman Jared Lee lost  nur to snap we hear it over and over  again if you've been transported to a  psych ward the shootings might never  happen there were clear warning signs  here to talk about the warning signs  indication we have been picking up some  signs we should be looking for  individuals once we know the outcome it  is easy to look back and perceive a  pattern that seems to be leading to a  common event often that's simply  hindsight bias if we put doctors in a  position of acting on behalf of the  government or acting on behalf of social  control then that undermines the  therapeutic mission restricting the  rights to people who are living with a  mental illness or possibly may be  diagnosed with the mental illness  just further perpetuates people not  receiving or seeking the treatment that  they need to get better and we know  prevention early intervention and  seeking that treatment right on the  onset is what supports people in  recovery so most people with mental  illnesses never do anything violent and  it's almost impossible to predict who's  going to snap without a prior history of  violence but still what's the harm in  taking precautions to answer that  question we turn to California  California's armed prohibited person  system aims to confiscate guns from  three groups those with a history of  violence wanted criminals and anyone the  state believes has a severe mental  illness because one nurse wrote false  information now I'm on a prohibited  persons list I've never done anything to  hurt anybody  Lynette Phillips and her husband David  have never committed a violent crime and  Lynette certai